00:56:12,631 --> 00:56:18,631
Dick Johnson Is Dead is a 2020 American documentary film directed by
Kirsten Johnson and co-written by Johnson and Nels Bangerter.

13
01:00:53,684 --> 01:00:59,684
The story focuses on Johnson's father Richard, who suffers from dementia, portraying
different ways—some of them violent "accidents"—in which he could ultimately die.

14
01:05:34,736 --> 01:05:40,736
In each scenario, the elderly Johnson plays along with his
daughter's black humor and imaginative fantasies.

15
01:10:15,789 --> 01:10:21,789
The film premiered at the 2020 Sundance Film Festival, where it won the
Special Jury Award for Innovation in Non-fiction Storytelling.

16
01:14:56,842 --> 01:15:02,842
It was released on Netflix on October 2, 2020.

17
01:19:37,894 --> 01:19:43,894
The film explores themes of dying and death, biography, alzheimer's
disease, stuntman, father daughter relationship.

18
